<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`RawLamToken` equality).** Equality of raw lambda tokens is decidable, by the boolean equality on those tokens.

**Definition (`lamAtomInsert` commutative).** Insertion of lambda atoms commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`lamFunInsert` commutative).** Insertion of function tokens commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`maxDepthInsert` commutative).** The binary maximum on depths commutes in its first arguments.

*Proof.* By commutativity of the maximum of natural numbers. □

**Definition (`LamToken` equality).** Equality of lambda tokens is decidable.

*Proof.* It is equality of the underlying raw tokens. □

**Definition (`lamForgetInsert` commutative).** Forgetful insertion commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`LamDToken` equality).** Equality of depth-bounded lambda tokens is decidable.

*Proof.* It is equality of the underlying tokens. □

**Definition (`lamDForgetInsert` commutative).** Depth-bounded forgetful insertion commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`RawLamToken`).** A raw lambda token is bottom, an atom, or a function token pairing a list of input tokens with a list of output tokens.


**Definition (`rawLamBEq`).** The raw lambda boolean equality.


**Definition (`rawLamListBEq`).** The raw lambda List boolean equality.


**Theorem (`rawLamBEq_eq`).** The equality raw lambda boolean equality eq holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`rawLamListBEq_eq`).** The equality raw lambda List boolean equality eq holds.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`lamAtomInsert`).** The lambda Atom Insert adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`lamFunInsert`).** The lambda function Insert adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


